+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * SDL2 at run time (Windows)
+ *
+ * XInput only knows Xbox-style controllers: a DualSense or DualShock 4 is
+ * invisible to it. SDL2 knows them all, but linking it would make every
+ * build depend on it. So SDL2.dll is loaded if it is there -- beside the exe
+ * or on the path -- and only the dozen functions used are looked up. With it
+ * loaded SDL reads every controller, Xbox ones included, and XInput is not
+ * polled; without it nothing changes. PAD_NO_SDL=1 ignores the DLL.
+ *
+ * The constants are SDL2's ABI (SDL_GameControllerButton and ...Axis).
+ * -----------------------------------------------------------------------*/
